<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Months-long Indonesia wildfires spew toxic haze across Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c43a2d94c13f5b07af84f89d0c9ab95081f25810cd99ad6c448bcfdd5b0c3fd</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T06:30:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261018-months-long-indonesia-wildfires-spew-toxic-haze-across-southeast-asia" /><summary type="html">Parts of southern Southeast Asia have been put under the highest-level haze alert as wildfires that have swept Indonesia for months continue to belch toxic smoke across the region. The seasonal wildfires are worse this year due to the drought conditions caused by a severe "super-El Nino" effect.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>India's 'cockroach' movement founder released from police custody</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6798c465144c894f066991f6d9fba27069331fb480bb67c2376e06e435753d73</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T05:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261018-india-s-cockroach-movement-founder-released-from-police-custody" /><summary type="html">Indian police released Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) founder Abhijeet Dipke from detention on Saturday after the activist was detained ahead of a rally calling for the resignation of India's chief election commissioner. Two other CJP leaders remain in custody after having been arrested while demonstrating at a protest site that police had ruled off-limits.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia's forest fires spark public health crisis across Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ddfe10bc4af9783f7f192bbf945e09f38c6fb35b11bc735bec4ec11305913f72</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:26:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261016-indonesia-s-forest-fires-spark-public-health-crisis-across-southeast-asia--ce92433485e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261016-indonesia-s-forest-fires-spark-public-health-crisis-across-southeast-asia" /><summary type="html">Massive wildfires in Indonesia show no sign of letting up. The environmental disaster is turning into a pollution crisis across Southeast Asia, as toxic haze from the blazes spread to neighbouring countries.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>Indian authorities detain 'cockroach' movement founder Dipke ahead of new protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e43fec6473533c65426b2fb44d6f739e6dc07647db6555bef3593c613fafd888</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T06:39:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261016-indian-authorities-heighten-security-close-park-ahead-cockroach-movement-rally--7b06e6dcb92a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261016-indian-authorities-heighten-security-close-park-ahead-cockroach-movement-rally" /><summary type="html">Indian authorities on Friday detained Abhijeet Dipke, the founder of the satirical youth movement "Cockroach Janta Party", ahead of a new protest in New Delhi, live images from the group showed. Police earlier closed a central New Delhi park in an attempt to stifle near-daily demonstrations calling for the election authority chief's resignation over the removal of more than 130 million people from voter lists.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan school roof collapse kills dozens of pupils, teacher in Peshawar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6d5e0aa906deb89b908610db369beea76eb4c9aa747fddb7122cd774e1c623d</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T08:02:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261015-pakistan-school-roof-collapse-kills-dozens-of-pupils-teacher-in-peshawar--9a905ed0517b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261015-pakistan-school-roof-collapse-kills-dozens-of-pupils-teacher-in-peshawar" /><summary type="html">A teacher and at least 32 pupils were killed when a school roof collapsed in the northwestern Pakistani city of Peshawar on Thursday, authorities said. At least twenty people were injured, three of them severely.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea test-fires submarine-launched cruise missiles amid rising tensions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8104b99040cdc8bd4014a757b4af81e660204cd51684f229fd7a77f20ac9966f</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T23:12:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-north-korea-test-fires-submarine-launched-cruise-missiles--e31421af3b62.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-north-korea-test-fires-submarine-launched-cruise-missiles" /><summary type="html">North Korea test-fired two types of submarine-launched strategic cruise missiles on Wednesday, state media KCNA reported Thursday, saying the launches posed no threat to neighbouring countries. The tests follow heightened tensions with South Korea after a September 21 landmine explosion in the Demilitarised Zone injured three South Korean soldiers.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>How far will 'Cockroach' movement go? India's youth-led protests defy Modi government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d9abb29c0ea1cba8675f86bb3fb25c9b3b303834517cf5f58fef245adbf569b</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T18:40:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261014-how-far-will-cockroach-movement-go-india-s-youth-led-protests-defy-modi-government--26fd7d79299c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261014-how-far-will-cockroach-movement-go-india-s-youth-led-protests-defy-modi-government" /><summary type="html">It all started as a bit of online satire by a few young people fed up by corruption. Clearly though, the "Cockroach" movement is no longer a laughing matter for India’s government, which has shut transport and blocked rallying points in the capital to quell the momentum of a youth-led mobilisation that's already brought down the education minister over rampant school exam cheating and is now spearheading the protests against the culling of names from voter rolls, with the electoral commission chief accused of bias.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>‘The idea that Modi must be feared because he holds all levers of power has gone out of the window’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20fd55295f0b8313406ef5dd799e99f0032b167c348bceab249312cdbfe9a947</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T16:51:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/the-idea-that-modi-must-be-feared-because-he-holds-all-levers-of-power-has-gone-out-of-the-window--88dfae3f38b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/the-idea-that-modi-must-be-feared-because-he-holds-all-levers-of-power-has-gone-out-of-the-window" /><summary type="html">Is Narendra Modi losing his most powerful political asset: the perception of invincibility? As India's youth protest movement confronts an increasingly combative government, Dr. Subir Sinha, Director of the SOAS South Asia Institute and Reader in Development Studies, argues that the political significance of the demonstrations extends far beyond the arrests of opposition activists and the growing confrontation between protesters and state institutions. Dr. Sinha examines how the government's increasingly repressive response may be exposing the fragility of its authority and institutional legitimacy. Could India's emerging protest movement be dismantling the political mythology that has sustained Modi's hold on power?</summary></entry><entry><title>Cheap weapons, growing fears: Inside the Taliban’s drone campaign against Pakistan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2dcb0535763549365e800552b62d27790afcaa0bcaaefb4d05bf04fe5866533f</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T12:52:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-taliban-suicide-drone-attacks-pakistan--4d38ee0ab100.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-taliban-suicide-drone-attacks-pakistan" /><summary type="html">Pakistan says it intercepted 23 suicide drones launched from Afghanistan into Pakistani airspace in September alone. Since the conflict began in February 2026, the Taliban have increasingly used drones to attack Pakistan, raising concerns in Islamabad.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>‘Dark day for Turkey’: Police halt broadcasts, make arrests in raid on opposition TV</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a405b588b0d23559a12c9fc8b85730261db8390700b075c2d3d3c05d11daeb60</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:09:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-dark-day-for-turkey-pro-opposition-tv-channel-boss-slams-police-raid-broadcast-halt--2027488a6f87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-dark-day-for-turkey-pro-opposition-tv-channel-boss-slams-police-raid-broadcast-halt" /><summary type="html">Turkish authorities appointed a government trustee to run popular broadcaster Halk TV on Wednesday after police raided its headquarters, halting live broadcasts and arresting 11 people. Halk chairman Cafer Mahirogluin denounced "a dark day for Turkey", adding that seven of his family members were among those detained.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Asia's fertility hub: Thailand emerges as top destination for IVF treatment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ca7f9cb0b03cfadbf69522005c25bbf1d59f3de0ac1b3bbc60a8e36a49ad91c</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T12:38:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261013-asia-s-fertility-hub-thailand-emerges-as-top-destination-for-ivf-treatment--bc3bbfd133c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261013-asia-s-fertility-hub-thailand-emerges-as-top-destination-for-ivf-treatment" /><summary type="html">Thailand has become one of Asia's leading fertility hubs. Every year, thousands of foreign patients travel to Bangkok's state-of-the-art private clinics for IVF, egg donation and other fertility treatments. They come from China, South Korea, Europe and across Southeast Asia, looking for what may be harder to find at home: shorter waiting times, lower costs and, in some cases, fewer restrictions.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>India’s youth-led Cockroach movement defies protest ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95bacd25a7581b348482d7df532b53353af75bd01dc4abb7ddfbc115ef7d606e</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T11:00:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/india-s-youth-led-cockroach-movement-defies-protest-ban--510cf1269e48.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/india-s-youth-led-cockroach-movement-defies-protest-ban" /><summary type="html">India’s youth-led Cockroach movement is intensifying protests against Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s government. Three leaders were detained after defying a ban at New Delhi’s Jantar Mantar protest site. Demonstrators are challenging a voter-list revision they claim favours Modi’s party, while the protests disrupt businesses across the capital.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands of Indians march to Supreme Court to oust election chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:613c64395086f8477aca13995ca5d83cfd10c6be2aa2f8648bad87a73ce115c2</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T16:23:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/thousands-of-indians-march-to-supreme-court-to-oust-election-chief--cfcf565f6afb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/thousands-of-indians-march-to-supreme-court-to-oust-election-chief" /><summary type="html">Protesters in New Delhi continue to take to the streets demanding the country's top election commissioner resign. Frustrations have been mounting after an investigation in a leading newspaper revealed concerns had been raised within the body, over the revision of voter lists. Delano D'Souza reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>India's opposition leader marches with thousands against election chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a052ce4ccd43973251cb1411e65ec713efe2269da308f3c93b8fc5d32dbb1ff2</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T15:14:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/india-s-opposition-leader-marches-with-thousands-against-election-chief--11dd429412fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/india-s-opposition-leader-marches-with-thousands-against-election-chief" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties and supporters of the so-called "cockroach" youth movement marched towards the country's Supreme Court on Monday, in the latest show of outrage against the recent removal of millions of names from voters lists. Critics say the move is likely to benefit Prime Minister Narendra Modi's ruling party – and are demanding India's election chief step down over what they describe as misconduct. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in New Delhi, Navodita Kumari.</summary></entry><entry><title>Five people missing as fresh flash floods hit central Nepal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0258f5846cec6de3ab2ec99ee705e0b6710bc094d5febb0c8094b34df6aa4ed7</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:43:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-five-people-missing-as-fresh-flash-floods-hit-central-nepal--2d9a2373d2a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-five-people-missing-as-fresh-flash-floods-hit-central-nepal" /><summary type="html">Nepali rescuers searched for five missing people on Monday, a day after new flash floods swept away more than 200 houses and five bridges along the Budhi Gandaki River. The country is still recovering from devastating floods, triggered by a mountain glacial collapse on August 26, which killed more than 1,400 people and left over 5,000 missing.</summary></entry><entry><title>Striking images show new flash floods hitting central Nepal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9eded444da874e3986c142f8c5815711ac258168a9f34a7280d9a4c83a44c66</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:14:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/striking-images-show-new-flash-floods-hitting-central-nepal--99e18aa6713c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/striking-images-show-new-flash-floods-hitting-central-nepal" /><summary type="html">Striking new images show new flash floods hitting central Nepal. This comes only six weeks after another disaster there left more than 1,400 dead and 5,000 missing. According to an initial assessment by the Nepalese authorities, at least five people are now missing. Elitsa Gadeva and France 2 have the details.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Illegal detentions' in India, as protesters allege foul play at Electoral Commission</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e107adfc9b9081e18c39e68a24c6d4a1326ed58f162027f4da572767c82c38b</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T10:51:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261012-illegal-detentions-in-india-as-protesters-allege-foul-play-at-electoral-commission--04511ed70d4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261012-illegal-detentions-in-india-as-protesters-allege-foul-play-at-electoral-commission" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, October 12: Widespread protests in India are met with detentions judged "illegal" by the country's Supreme Court. But first: Lebanese papers report as Hezbollah prepares for a new regional flare-up. Finally, Citroën hopes to win hearts and minds with an electric reboot of the vintage Deux Chevaux model.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Opposition leaders and journalists allege police abuses as fresh protests break out in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf54579575606c375a67d9e2684931161ec2360fc0d66d68ad6d56bc57e63d28</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T04:33:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-opposition-leaders-and-journalists-allege-police-abuses-as-fresh-protests-break-out-in-indi--008b7975f167.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-opposition-leaders-and-journalists-allege-police-abuses-as-fresh-protests-break-out-in-india" /><summary type="html">Indian opposition politicians and journalists alleged that police had been heavy-handed in cracking down in protests that swept New Delhi over the weekend in response to a nationwide voter roll revision that critics say disproportionately affects Muslim and other minority voters. Opposition leader Rahul Gandhi called for a fresh march to the nation's Supreme Court Monday.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Melbourne Islamic leader denies links to suspected FlyDubai hijacker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20a7bce2cacebe76e8757b2db22646603cd00fa41b9eca07db6a7d3c4189cb53</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T03:49:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-melbourne-man-linked-to-suspected-flydubai-hijacker-condemns-false-accusations--a41bc8875157.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-melbourne-man-linked-to-suspected-flydubai-hijacker-condemns-false-accusations" /><summary type="html">Abu Hamza, whose Melbourne-based Islamic community centre was linked by Emirati prosecutors to the suspect in the attempted hijacking of an Israel-bound passenger jet, publicly dismissed "false accusations" against him on Monday. While prosecutors alleged that the Omani co-pilot first became radicalised while studying in Australia, neither the community centre nor Hamza are accused of any criminal wrongdoing.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea fires multiple ballistic missiles off east coast, Seoul says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7da4b05f5d3aaee8c4aac7cf0ebbb2ba9a8c20073ba27021880d7a81e079b799</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T01:54:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-north-korea-ballistic-missiles-sea-japan-seoul--a82c58ea609e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-north-korea-ballistic-missiles-sea-japan-seoul" /><summary type="html">North Korea fired multiple ballistic missiles off its east coast on Monday, South Korea’s military said, amid tensions over border landmine explosions that injured three South Korean soldiers last month. Seoul said the missiles were launched from Pyongyang and increased surveillance, while Japan confirmed at least one suspected ballistic missile.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>India court orders release of 'cockroach' movement leaders after detention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f4a1e3635538928d92f7d81ed8236d245f5f4ba400cfca3dab5c5bd501619a86</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T05:45:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261011-india-court-orders-release-of-cockroach-movement-leaders-after-detention--14ab15b3b7ce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261011-india-court-orders-release-of-cockroach-movement-leaders-after-detention" /><summary type="html">An Indian court ordered the release of three leaders of the viral "cockroach" youth movement on Sunday, a day after their detention ahead of protests over alleged irregularities in voter-roll revisions. Upon his release, founder Abhijeet Dipke called Narendra Modi an "embarassment to India" in a social media post.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>India detains 'cockroach' leaders ahead of election protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f58d37f6263d51c2b68fef9ae52514161250a2ef8ef1885d29081b7c538b91a3</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T09:18:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-india-detains-cockroach-leaders-ahead-of-election-protest--da3c1675b34a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-india-detains-cockroach-leaders-ahead-of-election-protest" /><summary type="html">Indian police detained the head of the satirical "cockroach" online movement on Saturday, the group said, ahead of a major protest against the Election Commission that triggered strict security measures. Our correspondent Navodita Kumari tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Indian police crack down on 'cockroach' movement protest in New Delhi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d83569ce3f0619527ec14058f547ce4deaff0166e40b0da49452150ac757305b</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T06:37:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261010-india-s-cockroach-movement-chief-detained-ahead-of-major-protest--c11b066f94fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261010-india-s-cockroach-movement-chief-detained-ahead-of-major-protest" /><summary type="html">India's "cockroach" youth movement said Saturday that police had detained the group's leaders as well as "more than 15,000" protesters attempting to stage a major demonstration in the capital against the country's election commissioner following allegations of misconduct during voter-roll revisions.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>India protests grow over Election Commission mistrust</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:223de19bccf89c3ae63227a6fff9a6197bc4fdc877e9df1c88ed8a8099c86f85</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:08:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261009-india-protests-grow-over-election-commission-mistrust--fe5514facbb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261009-india-protests-grow-over-election-commission-mistrust" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Access Asia, we find out why multiple protests have broken out in India after an investigation by The Indian Express raised concerns about the integrity of the country's Election Commission. Journalist Faye D'Souza joins us to unpack how Narendra Modi's government is facing mounting pressure from the political opposition and the Gen Z-led Cockroach Janta Party. She also discusses the wider sense of discontent in India.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>India's dowry curse: Outlawed practice remains deeply entrenched</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:438eaff6f6fd445f3a461d5346f08a0a28d92e2c2f1d8e02413f8d8068f00650</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T12:19:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261009-india-dowry-curse-outlawed-practice-remains-deeply-entrenched--18ff855ec4f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261009-india-dowry-curse-outlawed-practice-remains-deeply-entrenched" /><summary type="html">India recorded 5,737 dowry-linked deaths in 2024, an average of around 16 women a day. Despite being outlawed more than six decades ago, the practice of dowry – the transfer or money or valuables from a bride's family when she gets married – remains deeply entrenched across Indian society. Our correspondents report.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>China's evolving funeral practices: From traditional burials to cremation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17dcb9ff1a75f02c626404630ff61b1bf89fbceb6d526c336dfa6ef777a8279c</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T13:39:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261007-china-s-evolving-funeral-practices-from-traditional-burials-to-cremation--52813773e1c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261007-china-s-evolving-funeral-practices-from-traditional-burials-to-cremation" /><summary type="html">This year, China released new rules for funeral practices. The government is putting an emphasis on affordable and environmentally friendly funeral services. It's part of a decades-long reform to promote cremation. But in a country where burials are deeply rooted in local traditions, how are these attempts to modernise funerals being perceived? FRANCE 24's Yena Lee reports.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>ICC unseals arrest warrants for Taliban education ministers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba132470d0c6d933ab9e72fee7599d30be086ee3f51745451f4fd5d58ecdfca0</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T16:16:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261005-icc-unseals-arrest-warrants-for-taliban-education-ministers--eef86bb29f9a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261005-icc-unseals-arrest-warrants-for-taliban-education-ministers" /><summary type="html">The International Criminal Court on Monday unsealed warrants for Afghan Education Minister Habibullah Agha, and Higher Education Minister Neda Mohammad Nadeem, accusing two senior Taliban officials of crimes against humanity for denying Afghanistan's women and girls over 12 their rights to an education.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Indian police detain demonstrators as protests over voter roll revision intensify</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d27010f9662489d6c6d176a93622f8065534413f59a8f8facb95007ce7bfe6b7</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T11:04:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-ndian-police-detain-demonstrators-as-protests-over-voter-roll-revision-intensify--4a3d03cb8d05.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-ndian-police-detain-demonstrators-as-protests-over-voter-roll-revision-intensify" /><summary type="html">Thousands of youth protesters and opposition supporters rallied in Delhi and Mumbai on Sunday to demand the resignation of India's election commission chief over changes to ​voter rolls as ‌police detained some demonstrators for a third day.</summary></entry><entry><title>North Korea launches ballistic missile as tensions with Seoul grow over border mine blasts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb9c98ed8aa6201e0182160a04cc3c1f7ba5026e0dbd698b6af9fbf9757cb505</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T02:40:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261003-north-korea-fires-ballistic-missile-after-seoul-s-apology-demand--31f42c33e2e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261003-north-korea-fires-ballistic-missile-after-seoul-s-apology-demand" /><summary type="html">North Korea launched a ballistic missile Saturday morning from the Wonsan area on its east coast into the Sea of Japan, according to South Korea's military. The launch comes amid renewed tensions between Pyongyang and Seoul, with the latter demanding an apology for a blast that wounded three South Korean soldiers inside the Demilitarized Zone last month.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>'Make our streets safer!' Mass women's protests sweep India over sexual violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd2a31df850e09ae913a1d701dec2172a5d57f0a6facf63b5e811441da535d42</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:57:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261002-make-our-streets-safer-mass-women-s-protests-sweep-india-over-sexual-violence--825117eadd3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261002-make-our-streets-safer-mass-women-s-protests-sweep-india-over-sexual-violence" /><summary type="html">In India, thousands of women have been taking to the streets calling for better protection of female students, following the suspected gang rape of a 17-year-old girl. The alleged incident in an upscale neighbourhood of New Delhi prompted authorities to beef up protective measures, but the women say limiting their access to public spaces is not the answer.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry></feed>
